{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-50813",
    "CVE-2026-50812"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that SQLite did not properly handle NULL pointer\ndereferences in the Session Extension when applying a corrupt changeset.\nAn attacker could possibly use this issue to cause SQLite to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-50812)\n\nIt was discovered that SQLite had a buffer overread in the Session\nExtension when processing a corrupt changeset. An attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-50813)",
  "id": "USN-8565-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in SQLite.",
